1 | devops | Fix PR 2829 on branch feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold, docs and infra half, per the comments on issue 2340 whose first lines read CRITIC W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD ROUND 2 and SECURITY W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD ROUND 2. READ BOTH IN FULL FIRST. ONE (critic B3, security N3): docs/operations/env-vars-iris.md gets a row for every env var services/iris reads (PORT, ENVIRONMENT, OLYMPUS_API_URL, ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI, IRIS_PUBLIC_URL, OLYMPUS_WEB_URL, IRIS_DENIED_HOSTS), the not-yet-read notes removed, the one-time bootstrap sets all of them with production values, and services/iris/.env.example mirrors every row; the doc must state that a missing IRIS_PUBLIC_URL or ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI fails closed and never falls back to localhost (wave 2 makes the code do that). TWO (critic N7): add .gitignore and .dockerignore to the bare-name list in scripts/hooks/scope-check.sh so devops can own them under services. THREE (critic F5): fix the CLAUDE.md sentence so it describes exactly what the hook enforces. FOUR (critic N5): README count of deploy workflows. FIVE (critic F6): the host-denied sentence in services/iris/internal/hostgate is user-visible copy with no section 9 row; add it to docs/prd/pages/assistant-channel.md section 9 as S11, marked PROPOSED, pending co-founder sign-off, with the exact text the code carries, and note in the PR body that it awaits the sign-off. VERIFY: make check-prd-index, the scope hook exercised on services/iris/.gitignore as devops (paste the exit), real exit codes. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Push to the same branch. | feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold

2 | go-backend | Fix PR 2829 on branch feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold, Go half, per the same two comments. READ BOTH IN FULL FIRST. ONE (critic F7): Iris must name the same authorization server the API names as its issuer; derive it from ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI exactly as apps/api/internal/handler/assistant_oauth.go does (one shared derivation rule, documented in both places), refuse to boot when OLYMPUS_API_URL and that issuer disagree, and add the critic test issuer_parity_test.go verbatim. TWO (security N1, critic N1 and N4): enforce the host deny list where the signature is verified: in apps/api, an ASSISTANT_DENIED_CLIENTS env var checked inside enforceScope (403 insufficient_scope) and in Refresh (invalid_grant), a token with no client_id claim refused on assistant paths, and in Iris the switch applied to every request including discovery and manifest, not only inside callTool, with an empty client_id denied; document ASSISTANT_DENIED_CLIENTS in docs/operations/env-vars-api.md is devops scope, so leave a one-line handoff note for it and the orchestrator handles it. THREE (critic B3 code side): a missing IRIS_PUBLIC_URL or ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI fails closed at boot in production, never localhost. FOUR (security N2): the kill-switch alert must not degrade to one line per request past 10,000 binding ids; bound the memory with an LRU or a time bucket. FIVE (critic N2): broaden the driver pattern in scripts/check-service-isolation.sh to catch a pure-Go driver, or add the third check as a go list based probe; this file is devops scope, so if the hook refuses leave a one-line note. SIX (critic N3): the Origin 403 answers with the same WWW-Authenticate challenge as other refusals, or the README states why not. VERIFY: go test ./... with the race flag in services/iris and apps/api, the critic tests green, real exit codes pasted in the PR body. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Push to the same branch, keep the PR a draft. | feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold

